  "dom_id": "step-q107255",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224461/assets/a8d41cd80424e11002d30b26ee1eec86e17f343a8bb9765013fced59e3e2885b.png)\n\nWhat is the volume of the cube?",
  "worked_solution": "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=4\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV=(4\\,\\text{cm})^{3}=64{\\text{ in}}^{3}.\n$$",
